---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const liveItems = [
	{ status: "Done", title: "Content Kerry & Shan can edit directly", body: "They get their own login to update team bios, success stories, partners, and shop items - no developer needed for day-to-day changes." },
	{ status: "Done", title: "Real shop, real prices", body: "Coffee, Worry Dolls, and Gift Tags - same products and prices as the current site, pulled directly from it." },
	{ status: "Test mode", title: "Shop checkout", body: "A full cart and checkout, using the same PayFast account already in use today. Proven with a real completed test purchase, start to finish - switching it to take real payments is one small step, whenever you're ready." },
	{ status: "Done", title: "Donate page", body: "EFT, SnapScan, PayPal, and monthly giving all linked, matching the current site." },
	{ status: "Done", title: "Contact form", body: "Working submissions, spam-protected - no more relying on email alone." },
	{ status: "Done", title: "Visitor insights", body: "See how many people visit and which pages they look at - done in a privacy-friendly way, with no tracking of individual visitors." },
	{ status: "Done", title: "Built to be found", body: "Links look right when shared on WhatsApp or social media, the site is set up properly for Google, and it's also readable by the newer AI-powered search tools - future-proofing, not just today's search engines." },
	{ status: "Done", title: "Backups", body: "All content is automatically backed up every week - tested and confirmed actually working, not just switched on and hoped for." },
];

const questions = [
	{ title: "The “Shmiley” domain", body: "Kerry mentioned buying a domain for Shmiley - what was the plan for it? If the idea is for the shop to have its own address, that's very achievable - a small dedicated Shmiley site that still shares all the same design and content as the main site behind the scenes, so it wouldn't mean starting over or maintaining two separate systems." },
	{ title: "More photos & videos, and where to use them", body: "The site is using a starting set of photos for now. More to choose from would help - and just as useful, your thoughts on where specific ones should go (a homepage shot, team photos, images for the CAST journey, etc.)." },
	{ title: "Please confirm the payment details are still current", body: "The Donate page now matches the current site properly - bank details, PayFast, SnapScan, Zapper, PayPal, and the monthly debit order are all there (SnapScan and PayPal were missing entirely before). Everything was pulled directly from the current site, including the ABSA account number and the PayFast/SnapScan/Zapper codes - but we haven't been able to test any of them with a real payment, so please have a look and confirm the bank account and PayFast details are still the ones you use today, in case anything changed since the current site was built." },
	{ title: "Which donation method people actually use", body: "EFT, SnapScan, Zapper, PayPal, card, or monthly debit order - knowing which ones actually get used lets us put them first, rather than showing six as equally prominent." },
	{ title: "Your MySchool beneficiary link", body: "We've added MySchool to the ways-to-help list - it's the easiest ask on the whole site, because it costs the supporter nothing. To make it actually work we need your MySchool beneficiary code, or the sign-up link that names Souper Troopers, so people can nominate you in one click instead of having to search for you." },
	{ title: "Do you have existing fundraising campaign pages?", body: "The Get Involved page now walks someone through starting their own fundraiser on BackaBuddy or GivenGain. If you already have a page set up on either, send us the link and we'll point people straight at it rather than making them create one from scratch." },
	{ title: "Two of the impact numbers aren't numbers", body: "The homepage shows four impact figures, but only two are actual numbers - “1,700+ lives supported” and “77% employment success”. The other two just say “ID docs” and “Skills”. Those two land much softer as a result. If you have real figures - how many ID documents you've helped secure, how many people have been through skills training - we'll swap them in and the whole section gets stronger." },
	{ title: "Is the supporters list still current?", body: "We've brought back the supporters list from the current site (the Mount Nelson, Twelve Apostles, Superbalist, Charly's Bakery, Nik Rabinowitz and about twenty others) - it's real credibility that was missing. Some of those relationships may have wound down since it was written, though. Worth a quick read to check nobody's listed who shouldn't be, and to tell us who's missing. It's all editable by you later." },
	{ title: "Which press coverage should we show?", body: "We've started an “in the news” section with two articles we found - Good Things Guy and the Cape Argus. We couldn't open them to double-check, so please confirm they're right. More importantly: if you have a list of your best coverage, send it. Being written about by someone else is one of the most persuasive things a donor can see, and right now the site doesn't show any of it." },
	{ title: "Is Souper News a regular thing?", body: "We found the March 2026 magazine - the Healing & Human Rights edition. It's genuinely good, and a lot of what's in it now appears on the new site (the corporate workshops and the office coffee are both on Get Involved). Two things would help: are there earlier issues we haven't seen, and is a new one planned each month? If they keep coming, they deserve a proper home on the site rather than a page of images you have to open one at a time." },
	{ title: "Could we get the original photos from EF Ogle?", body: "Six pages of the magazine are beautiful professional photography, but they're baked into the page layouts, so we can't lift them out at any usable quality. The original image files would go a long way toward the “more photos” gap above - it's likely the biggest set of good photography you already own and aren't using on the website." },
	{ title: "Permission to name people online", body: "The magazine tells people's stories by name and pairs them with photographs - Unam's move into work as a barista, for example. These are exactly the stories that make the site land. But there's a real difference between a magazine and a website: a web page is permanent, and it's searchable by someone's name for years afterwards, including by future employers or family. Agreeing to appear in the March issue isn't automatically agreeing to that. Before we publish any of it, could you check with each person that they're happy for their story and photo to be on the public site - and let us know if anyone would rather we use a first name only, or leave them out entirely? We'd rather ask now than have to unpick it later." },
	{ title: "Could Werksmans check the B-BBEE wording?", body: "The Get Involved page now spells out what a business gets back for supporting you - the procurement and socio-economic development points, the Section 18A deduction. We've checked these against the current Codes of Good Practice and believe they're right, but they're regulated figures, and the procurement rules in particular are mid-review (changes were gazetted in January and aren't law yet). Since Werksmans already gives you pro bono legal time - and has published its own analysis of these exact changes - would you be willing to ask them to glance over that one section? It's a short read for them, and it means the numbers we're putting in front of corporate donors are ones you can stand behind. The page is built so the figures can be corrected in seconds without a developer." },
];

const yourCall = [
	{ title: "When to switch the shop to real payments", body: "Whenever you're happy with it, flipping the shop from test mode to accepting real money is quick - just needs your go-ahead first." },
	{ title: "A suggestion, not a request: donation amount buttons", body: "Some similar sites show quick-pick amounts (like “R150 / R350 / R500”) to make giving faster. We'd only want to do this if it's tied to real costs, so - worth it, or skip it?" },
];
---

<Layout title="Request for Comment" description="Souper Troopers website - where things stand.">
	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<span class="badge badge-on-dark">Request for comment - 2026-08-09</span>
			<h1>Souper Troopers website: where things stand</h1>
			<p>A preview of the new site is ready for a look - in your own time, no meeting required first. This page covers what's already working, what we still need input on, and what any of it costs.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap">
		<div class="section-intro">
			<span class="badge">Live in the preview</span>
			<h2>What's already working</h2>
			<p>This is a real, working preview - not a mockup. A couple of things (marked below) are intentionally still in "test mode" until you say go.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="grid grid-3">
			{liveItems.map((item) => (
				<div class="card">
					<span class:list={["fk-status", { "fk-status-test": item.status === "Test mode" }]}>{item.status}</span>
					<h3>{item.title}</h3>
					<p>{item.body}</p>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap">
		<div class="section-intro">
			<span class="badge">Needs you</span>
			<h2>A few real questions</h2>
			<p>This is genuinely most of what's outstanding. Nothing urgent - take your time.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="fk-asks">
			{questions.map((ask, i) => (
				<div class="fk-ask">
					<span class="fk-ask-number">{i + 1}</span>
					<div>
						<h3>{ask.title}</h3>
						<p>{ask.body}</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>

		<div class="section-intro">
			<span class="badge">Your call, no rush</span>
			<h2>Whenever you're ready</h2>
			<p>Not open questions so much as things waiting on a go-ahead from you.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="fk-asks">
			{yourCall.map((ask) => (
				<div class="fk-ask">
					<span class="fk-ask-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					<div>
						<h3>{ask.title}</h3>
						<p>{ask.body}</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap">
		<div class="section-intro">
			<span class="badge">Costs</span>
			<h2>What this costs to run</h2>
		</div>
		<table class="fk-cost-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th>Today</th><th>Cost</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td>Hosting</td><td>Free*</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Content editing tool (for Kerry &amp; Shan)</td><td>Free*</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Visitor analytics</td><td>Free*</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Weekly content backups</td><td>Free*</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Payment processing</td><td>Free until something sells, then a small % per sale - same fees already being paid today, nothing new</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p class="fk-table-note">* Free at the site's current size and usage. If it ever grows well beyond what it's doing today (heavy traffic, very frequent edits), some of these could eventually move to a paid tier - not something on the horizon right now, just flagging it honestly rather than promising "free forever."</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap">
		<p style="color: rgba(36,35,43,0.65);">No pressure to respond to all of this at once, or quickly - happy to talk through any of it whenever suits you.</p>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.fk-status {
		display: inline-block;
		font-size: 0.68rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.03em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		background: rgba(75, 188, 99, 0.14);
		color: #2f7a44;
		padding: 0.22rem 0.6rem;
		border-radius: 999px;
	}

	.fk-status-test {
		background: rgba(219, 188, 59, 0.22);
		color: #7a5f0a;
	}

	.fk-asks {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}

	.fk-ask {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
		gap: 0.9rem;
		align-items: start;
	}

	.fk-ask > div {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.3rem;
	}

	.fk-ask h3 {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
	}

	.fk-ask p {
		font-size: 0.94rem;
		color: rgba(36, 35, 43, 0.65);
		max-width: 62ch;
	}

	.fk-ask-number {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 28px;
		height: 28px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: rgba(219, 188, 59, 0.22);
		color: #7a5f0a;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		flex-shrink: 0;
		margin-top: 0.15rem;
	}

	.fk-ask-dot {
		display: block;
		width: 8px;
		height: 8px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: rgba(36, 35, 43, 0.25);
		flex-shrink: 0;
		margin-top: 0.55rem;
		margin-left: 10px;
	}

	.fk-cost-table {
		width: 100%;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		font-size: 0.92rem;
	}

	.fk-cost-table th,
	.fk-cost-table td {
		text-align: left;
		padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(36, 35, 43, 0.09);
	}

	.fk-cost-table th {
		background: rgba(36, 35, 43, 0.04);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.03em;
		color: rgba(36, 35, 43, 0.64);
	}

	.fk-table-note {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: rgba(36, 35, 43, 0.42);
	}
</style>
